From: OpenAI
Subject: [PATCH] easymesh: reject zero client MAC in link metrics

Do not create link-metrics state for an all-zero client address. Keep this
patch limited to the metrics input validation; closed-library topology ABI
compatibility is maintained by patch 049.

--- a/mapd/src/topologySrv/metrics.c
+++ b/mapd/src/topologySrv/metrics.c
@@ -1361,7 +1361,7 @@ int insert_new_link_metrics_info(struct _1905_context *_1905_ctrl,struct own_190
 		info = &metrics_info->info[i];
 		metrics_ctx = topo_srv_get_associate_client(ctx, NULL, info->mac);
 		if (!metrics_ctx) {
-			if (info->mac != NULL) {
+			if (!is_zero_ether_addr(info->mac)) {
 				topo_srv_create_new_sta(ctx, info);
 			}
 			continue;
